  Worth flagging for anyone re-checking this page: the claim that enum values in
  item JSON are CamelCase and matched exactly ("DAMAGE" fails to decode) reads
  wrong from the enum declaration alone, whose constants are MAX_HEALTH_PERCENTAGE
  and DAMAGE. It is nonetheless correct. EnumStyle.detect returns LEGACY for those
  constants, which is what *builds* the camel keys, but the codec's own enumStyle
  is CAMEL_CASE, so getEnum takes the exact-equals branch against those keys rather
  than name().equalsIgnoreCase. All 93 shipped CostType occurrences write "Damage".
  This is the codec-chain rule applying to an enum — the case that looks safe.

docs/tasks.md (+23) — documented what task cleanup actually does: the unregister
action is exactly task.cancel(false), drained newest-first by PluginBase. Two
consequences that change how you write a task: `false` means do not interrupt, so
a running body (and a CompletableFuture.runAsync body in particular) continues to
completion and must poll its own stop flag; an unfired ScheduledFuture, by
contrast, is genuinely dropped. Added the `Registry is not enabled!` symptom for
registering after disable. Dropped a stale "build-12" reference.

